{
    "document_class": {
        "class_name": "interaction",
        "class_version": "3.1.0",
        "superclasses": [
            {
                "class_name": "statement"
            }
        ],
        "maturity_level": "stable",
        "abstract": true
    },
    "depends_on": [
        {
            "name": "time_reference_id",
            "mustBeNonEmpty": false,
            "documentation": "When the interaction happened, as one or more time_reference anchor documents. Required on interactions (Brainstorm J: an interaction tightens time to required). #52 (V_eta_time_reference_model_plan.md CHANGE 5): within this family every member describes THE SAME instant or extent, and `value.clock` on the REFERENCED document must be unique across the family -- that clock is what makes two members different; entries repeating one name (T15) are otherwise indistinguishable. Split-anchored intervals are NOT what a second member is for: they have no instance (every markvalidinterval call site passes one reference for both ends), so there are no `start_anchor`/`end_anchor` edges. Measured report-only, in batch, by did2.validate.silentLoss (`family_uniqueness_violation`); a per-document validator cannot see the referenced document and must not pretend to check it.",
            "must_refer_to_document_class": "time_reference",
            "multiple": true,
            "min_count": 1,
            "referent_unique_by": "value.clock",
            "ordered": false
        },
        {
            "name": "instrument_id",
            "mustBeNonEmpty": false,
            "documentation": "Optional: the device that performed the method \u2014 an instrument modeled as a subject (kind asserted via a term_assertion). The agent role; entity_id is the patient. Empty for hand measurements (D2).",
            "must_refer_to_document_class": "entity"
        },
        {
            "name": "software_id",
            "mustBeNonEmpty": false,
            "documentation": "Optional: the software that produced this value, modeled as a `software` entity (name + version + citation id). The agent of a computation; distinct from instrument_id (a measuring device) and from input_id (the input data, on calculations). Empty for hand/DAQ measurements; REQUIRED on calculations (calculation.require_inherited). Supersedes the v1 `app` block.",
            "must_refer_to_document_class": "entity"
        },
        {
            "name": "method_id",
            "mustBeNonEmpty": false,
            "documentation": "OPTIONAL: a named, shared `method` document this run used -- a protocol, a spike sorter's settings, a stimulus given as a recipe. The statement may ALSO carry an inline `method` whose `parameters` add settings only this run had: no variable in both, and the inline `term` empty (rule `method_shared_and_own`; Jess Haley 2026-10-22 [method shared plus own], replacing \"never both\", team 2026-08-09). A changed SHARED setting still makes a variant `method` document with `parent_id`. (`method_parameters_id` -> `method_parameters` until 2026-10-21.)",
            "must_refer_to_document_class": "method"
        },
        {
            "name": "acquisition_channels_id",
            "mustBeNonEmpty": false,
            "documentation": "The rig and channels this interaction was recorded on or delivered through -- v1's `devicestring` ('intan1:ai1-4,9'), as a shared `acquisition_channels` document (#73 item 56). OPTIONAL: present on interactions decomposed from an ingested epoch's probemap (recording observations, stimulator manipulations).",
            "must_refer_to_document_class": "acquisition_channels"
        }
    ],
    "file": [],
    "fields": [
        {
            "name": "method",
            "type": "structure",
            "blank_value": {},
            "default_value": {},
            "mustBeNonEmpty": false,
            "mustBeScalar": true,
            "mustNotHaveNaN": false,
            "queryable": true,
            "ontology": null,
            "documentation": "HOW it was done: `term` the technique and `parameters` the settings it ran with. The same block inline (here) and on a standalone `method` document (V_eta_method_plan.md, 2026-10-21). Used alone when the method and its settings have no name and id of their own in the source; otherwise the statement points at a `method` document by `method_id`, and an inline block beside it may only ADD settings only this run had, with an empty `term` and no variable the shared document also has (rule `method_shared_and_own`; Jess Haley 2026-10-22 [method shared plus own], replacing \"never both\", team 2026-08-09).",
            "constraints": {},
            "fields": [
                {
                    "name": "term",
                    "type": "ontology_term",
                    "blank_value": {
                        "node": "",
                        "name": ""
